# NGINX Gateway Fabric (NGF) — the NGINX implementation of the Gateway API, an ALTERNATIVE
# data plane to the self-managed Traefik v3. Deployed from the OCI chart
# oci://ghcr.io/nginx/charts/nginx-gateway-fabric (pinned in terragrunt) via the GENERIC
# shared/helm module, so this file is rendered with {namespace, environment, parameters}.
#
# Prerequisites (shared, already satisfied): the Gateway API standard-channel CRDs must exist
# BEFORE this installs — they're installed by the traefik-crds release. If you ever run
# nginx-ONLY (no Traefik), install those CRDs another way (NGF's own CRD kustomize / a
# standalone gateway-api release) instead.
#
# What the chart creates: the NGF control plane + a GatewayClass named "nginx"
# (controllerName gateway.nginx.org/nginx-gateway-controller). It does NOT create a Gateway —
# the routing module does (parameters.routing.gateways); NGF then provisions a data-plane
# nginx Deployment + LoadBalancer Service per Gateway (Klipper assigns the IP).
#
# Chart defaults suit the lab; this mostly documents intent + pins the class name.
nginxGateway:
  # The GatewayClass this controller owns. Gateways set gatewayClassName: nginx to use it.
  gatewayClassName: nginx
